          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Policies of Perestroika and Glasnost</strong><br>\nHis policies of perestroika (restructuring) and glasnost (openness) aimed to revive the Soviet economy and make the government more transparent. These reforms led to greater freedom of expression and some market-like reforms in the economy.</p>\n\n<p><strong>End of the Cold War</strong><br>\nGorbachev played a crucial role in ending the Cold War. He reduced the Soviet military presence in Eastern Europe and encouraged democratic movements, leading to the fall of the Berlin Wall in 1989.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Nobel Peace Prize</strong><br>\nFor his efforts in reducing East-West tensions, Gorbachev was awarded the Nobel Peace Prize in 1990, signaling international recognition of his global impact.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
