            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>The Dissolution of the USSR</strong><br>\nDespite his reforms, Gorbachev faced opposition at home. Economic troubles and nationalist movements grew, and in 1991, a coup attempt weakened his position, leading to the dissolution of the Soviet Union.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Later Years</strong><br>\nAfter resigning in 1991, Gorbachev remained active in social and political causes through his foundation and as an author, advocating for global peace and cooperation.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Gorbachev's Legacy</strong><br>\nGorbachev's legacy is one of significant reform in the Soviet Union, which eventually led to its collapse and the reshaping of political orders in many countries, influencing global politics well into the 21st century.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
